  "worked_solution": "First, the vector equation of the line is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -10 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -10 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-6t \\\\ -2t \\\\ t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5-6t \\\\ -10-2t \\\\ 2+t\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ Therefore, the parametric equations are:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=5-6t \\\\ y=-10-2t \\\\ z=2+t\\end{aligned}\n$$",
